    "growth_divergence_warning": "Equity CAGR (0.8-1.8%) diverges >30% from revenue (~6%) and EPS CAGRs: book value is held down by buybacks and dividends and was inflated by the 2015 Biomet stock deal; EPS CAGR (47.9% 3yr) runs off a depressed FY2022 GAAP base ($1.10) and FY2020 was a loss, so neither is usable. Revenue/organic growth selected.",
    "notes": "FCF CAGR is on the CSV basis (OCF - PP&E - SBC, which omits instrument additions): FY2020 1,018.8 -> FY2025 1,382.4 = 6.3%/yr. FY2022 OCF is missing from the CSV so the 3-year FCF CAGR is null. SBC (~1.1-1.4% of revenue) is small and stable, so SBC is not growing faster than cash flow."
