  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Zimmer Biomet stays the #1 hip/knee implant franchise growing roughly with a 4-5% procedure market but still losing a little knee share: organic growth of 3-4% (knees ~1-2%, hips ~4-5%, S.E.T. 4-6% as Paragon 28 foot & ankle compounds, Technology & Data double-digit from ROSA and Monogram), reported growth 4-4.5%. FY2025's deal and restructuring costs fade and GAAP EBITDA margin (pre-SBC) recovers from 27.7% to ~31.5%, still below the 33%+ peers earn. Cash conversion stays held back by ~7% of revenue in instrument sets and PP&E and an inventory-heavy working-capital model. Buybacks of ~$1B/yr keep the count flat.",
    "bull": "The innovation cycle finally lands: ROSA (knee, hip, and the new shoulder system) plus Monogram's semi-autonomous robot narrow the gap to Stryker's Mako installed base, the Persona/Oxford cementless knee portfolio stops the US share bleed, and the specialised US sales-force rebuild under the new Americas leadership lifts productivity. Organic growth reaches 5-6% for several years as S.E.T. (sports, extremities, Paragon 28 foot & ankle) and the ASC shift add mix, and EBITDA margin expands to ~33.5% on operating leverage and the end of serial restructuring.",
    "bear": "Mako-driven share loss in knees continues (ZBH knees grew 0.4% in Q2-26 against a mid-single-digit market), the US go-to-market reorganisation and repeated leadership turnover disrupt the sales channel, and China volume-based procurement plus European pricing compress international price. Organic growth settles at ~2.5%, special items keep recurring so margins drift to ~29%, and instrument capex rises to defend robotics placements. Exit multiple compresses to 13x as ZBH is valued as an ex-growth share donor."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Mature, cash-generative orthopaedic franchise with a durable installed base of surgeons and instrument sets, valued on owner FCF (company FCF definition, including instrument additions, less SBC) with an unlevered component build and 10-year horizon while margins recover from the FY2025 trough. The Metrics.csv FCF excludes ~$300M/yr of instrument additions and must not be used as the base.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Knee share loss to Stryker Mako continuing (knees +0.4% in Q2-26)",
      "US go-to-market rebuild and senior leadership turnover disrupting sales execution",
      "Recurring 'special items' (restructuring, integration, quality remediation, EU MDR) - margin recovery assumes they fade",
      "Pricing: China VBP, European tenders, US hospital/ASC pricing pressure",
      "Leverage ~2.9x net debt / EBITDA after Paragon 28 and Monogram; $1.2B current maturities in the next 12 months",
      "Terminal value carries most of the value; terminal cap multiple binds"
    ]
  },
