    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (dcf-methods routing row 1/2: US operating company, medtech/orthopaedics; no bank/REIT/holdco features, no live corporate action). Fresh build - no prior DCF or memory entry. FY0 = FY2025 revenue $8,231.5M; FY2026 growth set inside the August-2026 raised guidance (reported +3.9% to +4.9%; organic cc +2.25% to +3.25%; Paragon 28 adds ~110bps through April 2026). EBITDA margin is GAAP EBITDA + SBC (pre-SBC, after recurring special items): FY23 31.5%, FY24 31.0%, FY25 27.7% (Paragon 28/Monogram deal and integration costs, restructuring), H1-26 30.2%. Special items have recurred every year at ZBH, so the path is anchored to GAAP not 'adjusted'. D&A ~13% of revenue includes ~$666M/yr of acquired-intangible amortization (largely Biomet, much of it not tax-deductible) - the cash tax rate on EBIT (~32%) is therefore above the ~17-18% adjusted book rate: FY25 cash taxes $376.9M plus the ~$60M tax shield on $293M net interest, over unlevered EBIT ~$1.1B. Capex = PP&E + surgical instrument additions + acquired intangibles (FY25 224.5+300.5+52.4 = 7.0% of revenue). Working capital is a consumer of cash (inventories $2.27B + receivables $1.77B vs payables): wc_capture -35% of the revenue increase. Buybacks: $487M FY25, $500.8M H1-26, guided up to $1B for FY26 - the flat share count is being funded. Dividend $0.96/yr (~$190M). Metrics.csv FreeCashFlow excludes instrument additions; owner FCF here uses the company's own FCF definition.",
